{"seq":24,"slug":"sensation-perception","title":"感觉与知觉","stage":"DONE","category":"psychology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introMarkdown":"# 感觉与知觉\n\n把一束波长 700 纳米的电磁辐射射进眼睛，最终你「看见」的是红色——可宇宙里并没有红色，只有波长。这个从物理刺激到主观经验的跳跃，正是感觉与知觉这门学科要追问的核心：客观世界的能量如何被神经系统接收、编码，又如何被大脑重构成我们以为「就在那里」的现实。\n\n本 hub 沿着一条由方法到机制、由单通道到全局的主线展开，分四章递进。\n\n第一章「心理物理学基础」奠定整门学科的度量地基。在能谈论任何具体感觉之前，我们得先有办法把「主观感受」拴到「客观刺激」上：阈限是多少、刺激翻倍感觉会不会翻倍、人在噪声里究竟是「看见了」还是「猜对了」。韦伯-费希纳定律、斯蒂文斯幂定律给出感觉与刺激的定量关系，而信号检测论把「敏感性」和「判断标准」拆开——这套方法论会反复出现在后面每一章，是全 hub 的通用语言。\n\n第二章「视觉」以人类最主导的感觉通道，集中展示知觉的建构性。从视网膜的光转换、颜色的三色与对立机制，到深度、运动、形状如何被大脑从二维投影里推断出来，再到恒常性与错觉如何暴露这套推断系统的「先验假设」。错觉不是大脑的故障，而是它在用平时极好用的规则去解一道被精心设计成无解的题。\n\n第三章「其它感觉与多感觉整合」把视野从单通道扩展到跨通道。听觉如何在时间维度上解析频率与声源位置，化学觉与体感如何编码分子与接触，最后落到多感觉整合——大脑并非各感官各说各话，而是按可靠性给每条线索加权融合，这恰是一种贝叶斯式的最优估计。\n\n第四章「知觉的机制与前沿」回答「这一切如何统一」。注意决定了哪些信号被放大，预测编码与贝叶斯大脑提出一个颠覆性图景：知觉不是自下而上的被动接收，而是大脑用内部模型主动预测、再用感官输入纠错的过程。最后我们把这套理论带到 2026 年的技术现场——VR、感官替代设备与 AI 知觉系统，看它们如何既验证又利用大脑的建构本性。\n\n四章合起来回答同一个问题：物理刺激如何变成主观经验。从如何度量，到看得最清的通道，到跨通道融合，再到「大脑其实在预测」的统一框架——这是一条从现象走向机制的路。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"psychophysics","title":"心理物理学基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/psychophysics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-core-concepts","title":"感觉与知觉导论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/psychophysics/intro-and-core-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"psychophysical-methods-laws","title":"心理物理学方法与定律","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/psychophysics/psychophysical-methods-laws"},{"seq":3,"slug":"signal-detection-theory","title":"信号检测论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/psychophysics/signal-detection-theory"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"vision","title":"视觉","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/vision","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"visual-system-color","title":"视觉系统与颜色知觉","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/vision/visual-system-color"},{"seq":2,"slug":"depth-motion-form","title":"形状、深度与运动知觉","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/vision/depth-motion-form"},{"seq":3,"slug":"perceptual-constancy-illusions","title":"知觉恒常性与错觉","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/vision/perceptual-constancy-illusions"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"other-senses-multisensory","title":"其它感觉与多感觉整合","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/other-senses-multisensory","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"audition","title":"听觉","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/other-senses-multisensory/audition"},{"seq":2,"slug":"chemical-somatosensory","title":"化学觉与体感","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/other-senses-multisensory/chemical-somatosensory"},{"seq":3,"slug":"multisensory-integration","title":"多感觉整合","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/other-senses-multisensory/multisensory-integration"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"mechanisms-frontiers","title":"知觉的机制与前沿","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/mechanisms-frontiers","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"attention-and-perception","title":"注意与知觉","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/mechanisms-frontiers/attention-and-perception"},{"seq":2,"slug":"predictive-perception-bayesian-brain","title":"预测性知觉与贝叶斯大脑","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/mechanisms-frontiers/predictive-perception-bayesian-brain"},{"seq":3,"slug":"vr-ar-sensory-substitution-ai","title":"VR、感官替代与AI知觉","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/sensation-perception/mechanisms-frontiers/vr-ar-sensory-substitution-ai"}]}]}